.Dd February 1, 2026
.Dt DRIVER_OVERRIDE 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm driver_override ,
.Nm driver_blacklist_add
.Nd control driver binding policy
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/kern/driver.h
.Ft void
.Fn driver_override "struct device *dev" "const char *name"
.Ft void
.Fn driver_blacklist_add "const char *name"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn driver_override
function forces a device to bind only to a driver with the specified
.Fa name .
If
.Fa name
is
.Dv NULL ,
the override is cleared and normal matching rules apply.
.Pp
The
.Fn driver_blacklist_add
function adds a driver name to the global blacklist. Blacklisted drivers
are ignored during device matching, preventing them from automatically
probing devices.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
/* Force binding to "virtio-blk" */
driver_override(dev, "virtio-blk");

/* Prevent "legacy-ide" from loading */
driver_blacklist_add("legacy-ide");
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bus_match_device 9 ,
.Xr driver 9 ,
.Xr device 9
